{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":589,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","line":1037,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[$\\exp_p$ is a local isometry, so the radial lines are $\\exp_p^*g$-geodesics]\n\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric, def:dc-ch7-2-2, def:dc-ch1-2-2, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:3.4}\nFor $f=\\exp_p$ and the pulled-back metric $\\exp_p^*g$ on $T_pM$, every radial line\n  $\\gamma_v(s)=s\\,v$ is a geodesic of $\\exp_p^*g$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global}\n\n\\sketch The pullback construction makes $\\exp_p$ a local isometry. The image of $s\\mapsto sv$ is the geodesic $s\\mapsto\\exp_p(sv)$, and local isometries reflect geodesics, so the radial line is a geodesic for $\\exp_p^*g$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> is a local isometry, so the radial lines are <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p^*g$\">$\\exp _p^*g$</span>-geodesics] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d332d342d726179732d6172652d67656f646573696373\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-2</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Adc-ch1-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch1-2-2</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-expmap-global\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:3.4</span></span>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f=\\exp _p$\">$f=\\exp _p$</span> and the pulled-back metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p^*g$\">$\\exp _p^*g$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span>, every radial line <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _v(s)=s\\, v$\">$\\gamma _v(s)=s\\, v$</span> is a geodesic of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p^*g$\">$\\exp _p^*g$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-expmap-global\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global</a> </p><p>\\sketch The pullback construction makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> a local isometry. The image of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s\\mapsto sv$\">$s\\mapsto sv$</span> is the geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s\\mapsto \\exp _p(sv)$\">$s\\mapsto \\exp _p(sv)$</span>, and local isometries reflect geodesics, so the radial line is a geodesic for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p^*g$\">$\\exp _p^*g$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#rem:dc-ch7-3-4","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-2","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-2","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#rem:dc-ch7-3-4","title":"rem:dc-ch7-3-4","label":"rem:dc-ch7-3-4"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[$\\exp_p$ is a local isometry, so the radial lines are $\\exp_p^*g$-geodesics]\n\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric, def:dc-ch7-2-2, def:dc-ch1-2-2, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:3.4}\nFor $f=\\exp_p$ and the pulled-back metric $\\exp_p^*g$ on $T_pM$, every radial line\n  $\\gamma_v(s)=s\\,v$ is a geodesic of $\\exp_p^*g$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global}\n\n\\sketch The pullback construction makes $\\exp_p$ a local isometry. The image of $s\\mapsto sv$ is the geodesic $s\\mapsto\\exp_p(sv)$, and local isometries reflect geodesics, so the radial line is a geodesic for $\\exp_p^*g$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pullback-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-2","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-2","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/s